+"""Verified native finite-field problems from arXiv:2407.12688.
+
+The task is to invert one value of the paper's Theorem 3.5 permutation
+polynomial over GF(p^3).  A preimage is sampled first and the target is then
+computed, so generation never searches for the witness.  Verification is one
+exact polynomial evaluation.  The compact solution route is the Frobenius
+eigenspace decomposition behind Proposition 4.1; exhaustive inversion remains
+available as the deliberately disclosed Track-B reference algorithm.
