+Theorem 3.5 fixes the native family: for a in the norm-one subgroup, a != 1,
+and gcd(s,p-1)=1, f_5=A_a+A_(a^2)+Tr^s permutes F_(p^3).  Proposition 4.1
+and Table 1 in Section 4.1 supply its compositional inverse through the three
+local components.  The easy conditions that had to be avoided are stated in
+the same theorem: a=1 or gcd(s,p-1)>1 destroys the permutation promise.
